  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given two integers NNN and XXX. Your task is to construct a permutation PPP of {1,2,…,N}\\{1, 2, \\ldots, N\\}{1,2,…,N} which satisfies the following conditions:\n\n\nP1=XP_1 = XP1​=X\nLet DDD be the difference array of PPP, i.e, DDD is an array of length N−1N-1N−1 such that Di=Pi+1−PiD_i = P_{i+1} - P_iDi​=Pi+1​−Pi​ for 1≤i&lt;N1 \\leq i \\lt N1≤i&lt;N.\n\nThe array DDD should be a palindrome.\nIf there are multiple solutions, you may print any of them.\n\nIf there's no solution, output −1-1−1 instead.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of a single line containing two space-separated integers NNN and XXX.\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nFor each test case, output NNN space-separated integers representing the permutation PPP. If there's no solution, output −1-1−1 instead.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "3≤N≤4⋅1053 \\leq N \\leq 4 \\cdot 10^53≤N≤4⋅105",
      "1≤X≤N1 \\leq X \\leq N1≤X≤N",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 4⋅1054 \\cdot 10^54⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n3 2\n3 1\n4 3\n4 4",
        "output": "-1\n1 2 3\n3 1 4 2\n4 3 2 1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: There's no permutation satisfying the conditions.\nTest case 222: N=3N = 3N=3 and X=1X = 1X=1. Consider P=[1,2,3]P = [1, 2, 3]P=[1,2,3].\n\nP1=1=XP_1 = 1 = XP1​=1=X\nD=[1,1]D = [1, 1]D=[1,1] is a palindrome.\n\nTest case 333: N=4N = 4N=4 and X=3X = 3X=3. Consider P=[3,1,4,2]P = [3, 1, 4, 2]P=[3,1,4,2].\n\nP1=3=XP_1 = 3 = XP1​=3=X\nD=[−2,3,−2]D = [-2, 3, -2]D=[−2,3,−2] is a palindrome."
      }
    ]
